oracle: host CPython 3.11.17, 3.12.3, 3.13.16 (python3.11, python3.12, python3.13)
command: {python3.11,python3.12,python3.13} -I int_underscores.py
result: exit 0; stdout is exactly <name>.expect
releases: 3.11.17, 3.12.3 and 3.13.16 by their own host interpreters (above); 3.0a1 and 3.16.0a1 through the py3 profile's pinned-source evidence (python-iir-compiler/src/profiles.rs)
why: PEP 515 `_` separators (3.6+) and the zero spellings `00` and `0_0`
not 3.0a1: PEP 515 `_` separators arrived in 3.6, so 3.0a1's tokenizer (tok_get, Parser/tokenizer.c blob 776183d8) rejects `1_000`; see int_underscores.reject@3.0a1
